.TH SPEC2NII\-PHILIPS "1" "July 2024" "" "User Commands"
.B spec2nii\ philips
\(en convert from Philips spar/sdat format
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B spec2nii\ philips
.RB [ \-h ]
.RB [ \-t\ \fITAGS\  [ \fITAGS \ ...]]
.RB [ \-s\ \fISHAPE\  [ \fISHAPE \ ...]]
.RB [ \-\-special\ \fISPECIAL ]
.RB [ \-j ]
.RB [ \-f\ \fIFILEOUT ]
.RB [ \-o\ \fIOUTDIR ]
.RB [ \-\-nifti1 ]
.RB [ \-\-override_nucleus\ \fIOVERRIDE_NUCLEUS\  [ \fIOVERRIDE_NUCLEUS \ ...]]
.RB [ \-\-override_frequency\ \fIOVERRIDE_FREQUENCY\  [ \fIOVERRIDE_FREQUENCY \ ...]]
.RB [ \-\-override_dwelltime\ \fIOVERRIDE_DWELLTIME ]
.RB [ \-\-anon ]
.RB [ \-\-verbose ]
.I sdat
.I spar
.SH OPTIONS
.SS "POSITIONAL\ ARGUMENTS"
.TP
.I sdat
SDAT file.
.TP
.I spar
SPAR file.
.SS "OPTIONAL\ ARGUMENTS"
.TP
.B \-h\fR,\ \fB\-\-help
Show a help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-t\ \fITAGS\  [ \fITAGS \ ...],\  \-\-tags\ \fITAGS\  [ \fITAGS \ ...]
Specify NIfTI MRS tags used for higher (5th-7th) dimensions.
Defaults to
.B DIM_DYN
if more than one spectrum is present.
Can be used to create singleton higher dimensions.
.TP
.BR \-s\ \fISHAPE\  [ \fISHAPE \ ...],\  \-\-shape\ \fISHAPE\  [ \fISHAPE \ ...]
Specify the shape of higher (5th-7th) dimensions.
Applies numpy style reshaping.
.TP
.B \-\-special\ \fISPECIAL
Identify special case sequence.
Options:
.RB \(oq hyper \(cq,
.RB \(oq hyper\-ref \(cq.
.TP
.B \-j\fR,\ \fB\-\-json
Create json sidecar.
.TP
.B \-f\ \fIFILEOUT\fR,\ \fB\-\-fileout\ \fIFILEOUT
Output file base name (default = input file name).
.TP
.B \-o\ \fIOUTDIR\fR,\ \fB\-\-outdir\ \fIOUTDIR
Output location (default =
.BR . ).
.TP
.B \-\-nifti1
.TP
.BR \-\-override_nucleus\ \fIOVERRIDE_NUCLEUS\  [ \fIOVERRIDE_NUCLEUS \ ...]
Override
.B ResonantNucleus
field with input(s).
E.g. \(oq\fB2H\fR\(cq.
.TP
.BR \-\-override_frequency\ \fIOVERRIDE_FREQUENCY\  [ \fIOVERRIDE_FREQUENCY \ ...]
Override
.B SpectrometerFrequency
field with input(s).
Input in MHz.
.TP
.BR \-\-override_dwelltime\ \fIOVERRIDE_DWELLTIME
Override dwell time field with input.
Input in seconds.
.TP
.B \-\-anon
Create file without sensitive metadata.
For greater control use
.BR spec2nii\-anon (1).
.TP
.B \fB\-\-verbose
.SH "SEE\ ALSO"
.BR spec2nii (1)
.P
